      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>name is the name of the customer-managed encryption key to be used for disk encryption. The value should correspond to an existing KMS key and should consist of only alphanumeric characters, hyphens (-) and underscores (_), and be at most 63 characters in length.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>projectID</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>projectID is the ID of the Project in which the KMS Key Ring exists. It must be 6 to 30 lowercase letters, digits, or hyphens. It must start with a letter. Trailing hyphens are prohibited.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
